<title>BELGIUM: EU's Van Miert says satisfied with UK telecoms.</title>
<headline>EU's Van Miert says satisfied with UK telecoms.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert declined to comment on Thursday on the merger of British Telecommunications Plc and MCI Communications Corp but said he was satisfied with the liberalisation of the British telecommunications market.</p>
<p>Van Miert acknowledged that BT has a de facto dominant position in the British market, but told reporters: &quot;They are not misusing their dominant position. Competitors are given a chance in the British market.&quot;  </p>
<p>Under U.S. law a foreign company is only allowed to buy more than 20 percent of a U.S. telecommunications company if the Washington authorities deem the foreign company's market to be open.</p>
</text>
